# examples/games/04_top_down, played: worn down by the room, then out of the
# door with the room cleared.
#
# The character is on the arrows (TopDown, 240 px/s) and fires on Space
# (ui_accept) the way it last moved -- right, before it has moved at all. Five
# enemies come along the middle of the room at 90 px/s; one touching it costs
# a fifth of its health, and then it is safe for 0.8 s. A shot of its own
# never hurts it, and an enemy takes two. See tests/e2e/script.h for the
# grammar.

# --- the failure path: five touches -------------------------------------------

# Straight at them. The first touch is in frame 61, and the pile of them pushes
# back and keeps touching: one a 0.8 s, five in all.
1 press KEY_RIGHT
112 shot hurt
259 expect scene TopDownScene
260 expect scene OverScene
263 shot you_died

# Play again, with the mouse: down on 272, up on 273, the new room from 274.
270 release KEY_RIGHT
272 click 400 245
272 expect scene OverScene
273 expect scene TopDownScene

# --- the happy path: ten hits, and the door ---------------------------------------

# A shot every eighth frame from where it stands, straight down the line they
# walk along -- fourteen for the ten hits five enemies take -- and when the
# front ones are down, at the rest and on to the door: the last falls in frame
# 387, and the door is reached in 471, untouched.
